# Pairs with ProvenanceNoEmptyOrigin. Drops the #2621 normalisation: an
# unstamped (locally authored) write keys a per-origin high-water by the empty
# origin. In production the BackupOriginProvenance constructor then throws,
# which failed every full capture of a tree without replication.
MODULE: ProvenanceNoEmptyOriginDropsRule
TARGET: ProvenanceNoEmptyOrigin
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: an unstamped write contributes an empty-origin high-water (#2621)

--- FIND
StampedOrigins(I) == {log[i].stamp : i \in I} \ {""}
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the empty origin is not normalised away.
StampedOrigins(I) == {log[i].stamp : i \in I}
--- END
